# Data units. The bit `b` and the byte `B` (eight bits) take the SI prefixes,
# where `kB` is 1000 B, and the binary ones, where `KiB` is 1024 B. A rate
# needs no unit of its own: `MiB.s^-1`, `kb.s^-1`. A binary prefix and a `.` on
# its own is a scale, as `k.` is: `1Ki.` is 1024.

sheet Literals

| Name     | Value     |
| -------- | --------- |
| byte     | 5B        |
| bit      | 40b       |
| kilobyte | 1kB       |
| kibibyte | 1KiB      |
| memory   | 16GiB     |
| speed    | 100Mb.s^-1 |
| scale    | 1Ki.      |
| mebi     | 1.5Mi.    |

sheet Arithmetic

| Name        | Value                  |
| ----------- | ---------------------- |
| sum         | = 4GiB + 512MiB        |
| decimal     | = 1kB + 1KiB           |
| in bytes    | = 1KiB.to('B')         |
| in bits     | = 1kB.to('b')          |
| megabits    | = 125kB.to('Mb')       |
| downloaded  | = 10MB.s^-1 * 3s       |
| time to get | = 1GiB.to('MiB') / 50MiB.s^-1 |
| ordered     | = 1kB < 1KiB           |
| equal       | = 8b == 1B             |

# A column of data. `Information` is held in bytes unless it says another, as
# `Information[GiB]`, in which a cell written in any unit is shown, and a bare
# number is read.
sheet Disks

Disk : String
Size : Information[GiB]
Free : Information[GiB]

| Disk   | Size  | Free   |
| ------ | ----- | ------ |
| system | 512GiB | 120GiB |
| data   | 2TiB   | 1.5TiB |
| backup | 4000   | 3500   |

sheet Totals

| Name  | Value                 |
| ----- | --------------------- |
| size  | = Disks.Size.sum()    |
| free  | = Disks.Free.sum()    |

# Data over an area, as a disk drive's: `InformationDensity` holds `b.m^-2`.
sheet Drives

Drive   : String
Density : InformationDensity[Gb.m^-2]

| Drive | Density     |
| ----- | ----------- |
| old   | 100Gb.m^-2  |
| new   | 1TB.m^-2    |
| bare  | 500         |

